```
Reason:
The code attempts to allocate memory using `kmalloc` without checking if the allocation was successful. If `kmalloc` fails, `rctx->ext` will be `NULL`, but the code continues to set `subreq->cryptlen` based on the potentially invalid allocation size, leading to an out-of-bounds write when `pre_crypt()` accesses the embedded buffer.

